# Constellation stick figures, written by hand in terms of Bayer / Flamsteed designations.
# gen_assets.py resolves each designation against the Yale Bright Star Catalogue (bsc5.dat) and
# writes app/src/main/assets/constellations.txt, which refers to stars by HR number.
#
# Line format:  Abbr | Name | Genitive | polyline / polyline / ...
#   Abbr       IAU three-letter abbreviation, as used in the BSC (column 12-14).
#   Name       label shown in the sky view.
#   Genitive   used when naming stars ("alpha Canis Majoris").
#   polyline   star designations joined by '-'. Consecutive stars are connected by a line.
# Star designations:
#   Alp, Bet2, Pi3     Bayer letter (Greek abbreviation as in the BSC) with optional superscript,
#                      in the figure's own constellation
#   Alp And            Bayer letter in another constellation (a shared star)
#   61, 24 Cap         Flamsteed number (own constellation, or the one named)
#   #1234              raw HR number
# A designation shared by a close pair (e.g. Alp Gem) resolves to the brighter component.

